<[scott] S.W.SQUIRES>   ga
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> ok
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> I personally feel, we have given free accounts...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> to the people who are contributing...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> if people don't think the time is work the cost...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> then I can't deal with them...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> it is not going to get any better....
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> and even now the cost to sign up as gone up...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> what will they do when it cost 6/hr or $10/month?
<JAX>
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> I can not make that decision for them.
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> ga jack
<JAX> If GEnie raises the ante past an extra 50 cents an hour ...
<JAX> I will send them one of my famous flames and log off ...
<JAX> we should, in that case, move to the WELL or better yet ...
<JAX> start our own system ...
<JAX> there are some of us ...
<JAX> who have a bit of trouble with the idea of the FIG enriching GE ...
<JAX> a notorious corporate bad citizen ...
<JAX> and if they raise their rates, in my case, that would be the last straw ..
<JAX> as far as freebies, I didn't mean to imply ...
<JAX> that one-time guests like Johns Hopkins shouldn't get on free ...
<JAX> of course they should ...
<JAX> but if FIG has the money to blow ...
<JAX> they should improve their office staff, who don't even answer Email ...
<JAX> they receive on GEnie.
<JAX> ,
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> ok
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> the ante (if raised) won't be for GEnie alone...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> but done by the FCC who is still trying to...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> take away the advantage the "enhanced services"...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> get over "normal" long distance rates...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> and $10/month has been tossed around...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> quite a bit recently, but ...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> no matter what, guest speaker will always...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> be able to get a free account...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> for the time they are speaking...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> after that, it has to be up to them to...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> continue to "use" us...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> FIG does NOT have a bunch of money...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> to spend on provinding a service...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> instead these information services...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> pay us to draw people to use their systems...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> it is they who have to justify the size...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> of the system, and provide it's maintenance...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> FIG does not have the money to do all that...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> but we do have the volunteers to open up...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> services like this.  Another one is in the...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> works right now, or so I've heard...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> so I guess, we just spread ourselves out...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> and be happy with the users we've got...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> I think we will draw more still...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> we are only about 7 months old...
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> and it will take a while longer to reach everybody.
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> we'll see what one year brings.
<JAX>
